<section class="placer-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="placer-prose">
      <h2>What is placer mining equipment?</h2>
      <p><strong>Placer mining equipment</strong> is the gear used to separate gold from loose surface deposits - sand, gravel, and clay - instead of hard rock. In placer (or <a href="/blog/alluvial-vs-hard-rock-gold-mining-equipment/">alluvial</a>) gold mining, the gold is already free; the job is to wash away the worthless material and trap the gold. The machine that does this is a <a href="/products/">gold wash plant</a>, and it is the centerpiece of nearly every commercial placer gold operation on earth.</p>
      <p>A modern wash plant replaces three separate pieces of equipment - a screen, a trommel, and a sluice box - by combining a grizzly intake, classification, and a high-recovery sluice into one portable, ready-to-run unit. Feed it with an excavator or loader, add water, and it recovers gold at <strong>95-98%</strong> with no mercury.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="placer-section cream">
  <div class="container">
    <div style="text-align:center;max-width:680px;margin:0 auto">
      <h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:2rem;color:var(--black)">Types of Placer Gold Mining Equipment</h2>
      <p style="color:var(--gray-500);margin-top:12px">How the common pieces of placer mining equipment fit together - and why a wash plant does most of the work.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="equip-grid">
      <div class="equip-card">
        <div class="equip-icon">{{ icon("factory", 24) }}</div>
        <h3>Gold Wash Plants</h3>
        <p>The all-in-one workhorse: grizzly, classification and sluice in one unit. <a href="/products/" style="color:var(--gold-dark);font-weight:600">Our 50-300 TPH models</a> are the core of a placer setup.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="equip-card">
        <div class="equip-icon">{{ icon("target", 24) }}</div>
        <h3>Trommels</h3>
        <p>A rotating drum that screens and breaks up material. Built into every one of our wash plants - see <a href="/blog/gold-wash-plant-vs-trommel/" style="color:var(--gold-dark);font-weight:600">wash plant vs trommel</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="equip-card">
        <div class="equip-icon">{{ icon("bolt", 24) }}</div>
        <h3>Sluice Boxes</h3>
        <p>Where gold is actually captured. Our mercury-free sluice design recovers <a href="/blog/fine-gold-recovery/" style="color:var(--gold-dark);font-weight:600">fine gold down to 200 mesh</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="equip-card">
        <div class="equip-icon">{{ icon("wrench", 24) }}</div>
        <h3>Classifiers &amp; Screens</h3>
        <p>Sort material by size before recovery so the sluice runs efficiently. Integrated into the wash plant, not a separate purchase.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="equip-card">
        <div class="equip-icon">{{ icon("pickaxe", 24) }}</div>
        <h3>Highbankers &amp; Sluices</h3>
        <p>Small-scale, hand-fed gear for prospecting. Great for sampling - but a wash plant is what you scale to for production.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="equip-card">
        <div class="equip-icon">{{ icon("leaf", 24) }}</div>
        <h3>Concentrators</h3>
        <p>A final-stage clean-up for the very finest gold. Pairs with a wash plant to push recovery even higher on flour-gold ground.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

