      <h2>How to choose placer mining equipment</h2>
      <p>The right setup comes down to how much material you move per hour and how portable you need to be:</p>
      <h3>Small claims &amp; prospecting</h3>
      <p>A <a href="/products/50-ton/">50 ton-per-hour wash plant</a> is highly portable, sets up in under 30 minutes, and is the best seller for individual claims and <a href="/blog/small-mining-operations/">small mining operations</a>.</p>
      <h3>Growing &amp; commercial operations</h3>
      <p>The <a href="/products/100-ton/">100</a> and <a href="/products/200-ton/">200 ton-per-hour</a> plants handle serious volume while staying movable. The 200 is our commercial best seller.</p>
      <h3>Large-scale production</h3>
      <p>The <a href="/products/300-ton/">300 ton-per-hour</a> plant is built for high-volume, large-scale alluvial operations. Not sure which fits? See the <a href="/products/">full model comparison</a> or read our guide to <a href="/blog/choosing-right-size-gold-wash-plant/">choosing the right size</a>.</p>
